      "id": 1,
      "text": "Willington takes its name from the willingness of local Huguenots and Presbyterians to worship and attend school together.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.scpictureproject.org/mccormick-county/willington.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Willington Academy was founded in 1804 and educated many of the South's future leaders, including eleven governors.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.scpictureproject.org/mccormick-county/willington.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Willington grew at its present location due to the establishment of the Savannah Valley Railroad during the mid-1880s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://mccormickscchamber.org/what-to-do/historic-railtowns/willington/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Calhoun-Gibert House and Guillebeau House in Willington are listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
